  "steps": [
    {
      "text": "In a large bowl, combine milk powder, non-dairy creamer, vanilla flavored creamer, sugar and instant tea. Stir in ginger, cinnamon, cloves and cardamom. In a blender or food processor, blend 1 cup at a time, until mixture is the consistency of fine powder.",
      "group": null
    },
    {
      "text": "To serve: Stir 2 heaping tablespoons Chai tea mixture into a mug of hot water.",
      "group": null
    }
  ],
  "footnotes": [],
  "nutrition": null,
  "importedNotes": [
    {
      "text": "*You may choose to omit the French vanilla creamer, and use 2 teaspoons vanilla extract instead. To do so, mix the vanilla into the sugar, let it dry, then break the sugar into small lumps. Follow the same procedure as above."
    },
    {
      "text": "I cut the sugar down a third, though. It was a little sweet for my personal tastes."
    },
    {
      "text": "I have decreased the sugar by 1/3, to just one cup and in the future I will probably eliminate the French vanilla creamer and just add powdered vanilla (vanilin)."
    },
    {
      "text": "This recipe matches the taste perfectly (except I cut the sugar back to 1 1/2 cups). Don't be put off by the expense of the cardamom -- it's worth it. If using a blender, mix ingredients with a fork first, then blend only about a cup and a half at a time. Also, be sure to blend it really well (because the spices can get kind of chunky in your drink)."
    },
    {
      "text": "I use 1 and 1/2 cups of Splenda. I also add nutmeg, coriander and allspice. Great with water, fantastic with milk."
    }
  ],
